        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(whatsapp): preserve bot-authored quote replies",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a user replied to an OpenClaw-authored WhatsApp message, the gateway could not reconstruct that outbound message as a self-authored quote. WhatsApp Desktop then lost the native reply bubble.\n\nRefs #91445.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe repaired branch records the existing bounded quote metadata immediately after Baileys accepts an outbound send. It stores only `fromMe` and preview text; pinned Baileys derives the quoted self participant from its `userJid`, so the earlier self-JID/LID synthesis was removed.\n\n## User Impact\n\nReplies to bot-authored WhatsApp messages retain the native quoted-reply context, including the Desktop reply bubble.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Quoted-message suite: 5 tests passed.\n- Actual outbound-cache regression: 1 passed, 80 unrelated tests skipped.\n- Pinned Baileys contract regression proves `fromMe` quotes derive participant from `userJid`.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Exact prepared head: `2b2770b36955cad2abffee34cc9dcb480c4dbd64`.\n- Gap: no live WhatsApp Desktop swipe-reply capture was available; hosted exact-head CI remains the merge gate.\n",
        "branch": "fix/91445-cache-outbound-quote-meta",
